  "upstream": {
    "package": "motion",
    "version": "13.2.0"
  },
  "surface": "Core surface: `motion.<tag>` (animate, gestures, variants with propagation/stagger, drag, layout basics), `AnimatePresence`, `MotionConfig`, live `useReducedMotion`, reduced-motion enforcement, `LayoutGroup` layoutId namespaces, `LazyMotion` with `domAnimation`/`domMax`, the `m` proxy and complete `./react-m` named host entry, plus the motion-value hooks (`useMotionValue`, `useScroll`, `useTransform`, `useSpring`, `useAnimate`, `useMotionValueEvent`); motion-dom's animation engine and gesture primitives are reused verbatim.",
  "divergences": [
    "Exit animations run via cleanup-before-detach instead of React's deferred-deletion machinery.",
    "`layout`/`layoutId` use single-element FLIP, not the full projection tree.",
    "An `initial` target without an `animate` target does not materialize inline initial styles; set the starting style explicitly or provide an animation target."
  ],
  "ssr": "Dedicated Node-mode tests verify deterministic hook initialization without DOM effects; Chromium verifies hydration adopts that output and unmounts cleanly. Motion host-component SSR remains unsupported.",
  "verified": "2026-09-13",
  "notes": [
    "Not yet ported: nested/shared layout projection (incl. child scale correction and shared layout during drag), drag momentum + elastic physics, the `useTransform` output-map form, and `when: 'beforeChildren' | 'afterChildren'` sequencing.",
    "motion 13.2.0 re-exports the same framer-motion release. Native MotionConfig supports scoped isValidProp inheritance and overrides.",
    "The complete pristine oracle passes 870 cases; five upstream cases are adapted one-for-one. Other native behavior is covered by separate conformance and differential tests; this is not a complete React Motion port.",
    "Native hosts animate DOM targets without writing back to external style MotionValues; component onUpdate/onAnimationStart and gesture callback/priority APIs remain unsupported.",
    "useTransform replacement input/range identities and Motion 13.2.0 unit-string springs with skipInitialAnimation remain limitations. See UPSTREAM.md and the complete case crosswalk."
  ],
